rsa-decrypt-key-handle-type: TPM2_RSA_Decrypt rejects TPM_RH_NULL with TPM_RC_VALUE

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, TPM2_RSA_Decrypt, Table "TPM2_RSA_Decrypt
Command", Handles): "TPMI_DH_OBJECT | @keyHandle | RSA key to use for
decryption" (no '+', so TPM_RH_NULL is not a member). Part 3, "Handle Area
Validation": "The TPM shall successfully unmarshal the number of handles
required by the command and validate that the value of the handle is
consistent with the command syntax. If not, the TPM shall return
`TPM_RC_VALUE`."

The keyHandle of TPM2_RSA_Decrypt is a TPMI_DH_OBJECT without '+' (Part 3,
TPM2_RSA_Decrypt), so TPM_RH_NULL must be rejected while unmarshaling the
handle (TPM_RC_VALUE + TPM_RC_H + TPM_RC_1, as tpm-rs and ibmswtpm2 return).
Version 185 unmarshals it as TPMI_DH_OBJECT+ and thus accepts TPM_RH_NULL
(and fails later with TPM_RC_AUTH_MISSING). Found by differential fuzzing.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl b/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/include/private/CommandDispatch.inl
@@ -1269,7 +1269,10 @@
 #define CURRENT_TPM_COMMAND RSA_Decrypt
 MAKE_DISPATCH_TABLE(
     // Command input handles
-    MAKE_INPUT_DISPATCH_ENTRY(MARSHAL_ID_TPMI_DH_OBJECT_Plus, keyHandle),
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // keyHandle is a TPMI_DH_OBJECT without '+' (Part 3, TPM2_RSA_Decrypt), so
+    // TPM_RH_NULL is TPM_RC_VALUE.
+    MAKE_INPUT_DISPATCH_ENTRY(MARSHAL_ID_TPMI_DH_OBJECT, keyHandle),
 
     MAKE_DISPATCH_SEPARATOR(START_INPUT_PARAMETERS),
     // Command input parameters
